0010: Render target 0 is the implicit swapchain's back buffer 0 object (internal 0016): GetRenderTarget(0) and GetBackBuffer(0, 0) return the same IDirect3DSurface9, as in d3d9 and DXVK. Upstream made a separate place-holder linked to the back buffer (LinkBackBuffer), so code that compares the two by pointer (Apex Radiance's PostScene) never saw the scene and drew a black picture (Sims3-ApexRadiance#59). The back buffer is not counted as an implicit reference to the device: it references the swapchain, and counting it made a new device's first AddRef and Release (a CreateDevice hook, such as the Windows compatibility layer's) destroy the implicit swapchain, so the next GetBackBuffer or Present read a null swapchain.

The server no longer holds a reference on a back buffer it maps for IDirect3DSwapChain9_GetBackBuffer or IDirect3DDevice9Ex_GetRenderTarget: the client only unlinks a back buffer, so that reference was never released. Upstream released back buffer 0's references by accident, through the destroy of its place-holder. Without the place-holder they stayed, and on a DXVK server every Reset failed ("device still has alive losable resources: 1"), the device stayed lost (resolution change, Alt-Tab). Upstream has the same leak for back buffer 1 and later.

Applies after 0001-0009 on NVIDIAGameWorks/dxvk-remix f35b86a (bridge/ only).

